Title:          jgmenu.tcz
Description:    menu generator for X11, also supports keyboard inputs
                Runs on wayland with xwayland enabled 
Version:        4.7.0
Author:         Johan Malm & contributors
Original-site:  https://github.com/jgmenu/jgmenu
Copying-policy: GPL v 2
Size:           152K
Extension_by:   aus9 @linuxquestions.org
Tags:           menu 
Comments:       Tested on icewm and sway. 
                On first load you get ~/.config/jgmenu/jgmenurc with only stay alive
                turned off by me. This means menu will exit gracefully. 

                How to use 
                ########## KB=keyboard
                menu can be used as a cascading menu = normal or
                by inputting keys which automatically converts to search mode.
                
                On first load you also get ~/.local/bin/pointer command
                
                KB shortcut is easier, I show the terminal command first
                run $ pointer #--- do not press enter yet.
                Move your cursor to a position on the screen you prefer. 
                This will be where the "normal" menu top left hand corner appears.
                Press enter in the terminal -> cascading "normal" menu appears 
                2) If your desktop supports KB shortcuts create an unused one to launch  
                   pointer eg on icewm key "Alt+b" pointer  
                3) If you have a lot of apps loaded, mouse may be faster but you can 
                   go into search mode by typing executable name 
                   Typing unknown value will report empty list
                4) eg inputting cp (for cpanel) brings up one hit=Control Panel
                    but to bring up apps...use pp as inputting ap fails for me. YMMV   

                 KB hints---assuming no mouse detected etc
                 #########
                 However you launch jgmenu, when menu appears, without a mouse you need 
                 to get "focus" into that menu. This how I do it ...press the space key
                 so menu goes into search mode and reports "empty list"
                 (Of course you can start typing the executable name too here)
                 Next press Escape....which takes you from search mode to normal mode.
                 Now you can use down arrow to navigate down thru the menus or 
                 right arrow to peek into each menu and use left arrow to come back
                 If you see your target press enter against it.
                
                 Pressing ESCAPE when you are in "normal" menu mode will exit the menu
                 ... no matter where you are in the menu

